o and four we were  almost gonna do like three and five like  how did that get figured out  no actually you know what's funny it was  deep after we like we were already um  deep in the production when we talked to  muhammad we're like why do we have two  and four we were just presented with two  and four and honestly the answer is very  very boring there was like kind of  logistical calendar reasons and all of  that um and because have you seen the  episodes  okay and so you know without without  giving things away for people who  haven't but um four is in many ways  location wise it's very much its own  thing you know and so it was able to be  something that we were able to cordon  off a little bit episodes one and two  talk to each other a little bit more but  um but that was kind of as we were  figuring out the production  um and again you'll see with five and  six uh again very much their own voice  from each from each other and from the  rest of the episodes so that was pretty  much why is that um that each episode  has its own voice and we were handed two  and four  do you think it's do you think moonlight  has obviously never been done in live  action before like this is the first  time he's being brought into the mcu do  you feel like that's easier or harder  when a character like this you know when  you sort of have free reign to create  you know you know  it it's not that it's easier or harder  in terms of  telling the story you want to tell with  this character what what does come with  it that's a little bit difficult is that  it's the pressure to get it right i  suppose is a little higher because it  hasn't been done yet and also with a  character that is  that is rightfully so as beloved as moon  knight and beloved for being something  different and  that comes with its its own set of  pressures you just want to make sure you  get it right but in terms of  of of telling a story using a character  that doesn't have a live-action  pre-established mythology that was  actually it was easier in some ways  and also  50 years of great comic books to draw  from  inspiration if nothing else it could be  as simple as like just a piece of  artwork we loved from one that would  inspire a whole shot um  [Music]  but uh  but yeah i mean it was if any i guess in  some ways it was a little bit  easier him not having a live action  pre-established anything yeah i mean  you've seen all of our all i think all  of our independent features all of those  share a universe so the idea of working  within a shared universe comes weirdly  second nature to us  but um  but really it was it was way just more  exciting i think just just very very  exciting that that  that there were no  boundaries to what he had to be you know  nowhere where he had to fit  also  oh sorry i also say also having these  not only just i mean everyone knows that  oscar isaac and ethan hawk are some of  the greatest actors of our generation um  but  they are also  great novelists and filmmakers and  screenwriters and to to be in a  situation where they could take some  sort of personal authorship over the  creation of these live-action characters  well i mean that's you got you got two  of the best we've got right now doing  that and so that that was exciting  uh before i run into time with you since  we're talking marvel i might as well  bring up loki um how did you guys uh  hook up for that  um  i mean we're still kind of even  processing uh being being handed  that job you know um but i suppose uh  you know what we can say about it um is  that uh we're really really proud of  what we've done on moon night and i  think that uh that marvel really likes  what we're able to do on moon night and  so we're hoping to kind of take all the  lessons that we learned which are  infinite  you know the  unbelievable amount of of uh of life  experience and and craft and art that we  uh that we made in moon knight and we  want to take all of that and kind of  bundle it back together um as we leave  loki  also it's also nice to be tackling  another character  in the mcu who is defined by  by being  um being different than the rest of the  pack and another outcast yeah they all  have complexity but but these two have  complexity and being outcasts and  there's something about that that feels  very special and an honor to tackle  cool thank you so much and seriously  congrats thank you it's good seeing a  familiar face today  you
 

